-- Daily expenses: a receipt kept with an expense, and an expense that names nobody.
-- track: C
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / constraint statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/daily-expenses/schema.ts and src/modules/cash-bank/schema.ts. The sections marked
-- "hand-written" are not managed by Drizzle. Reverse with the file of the same name in
-- drizzle/down.
--
-- Why: the founder asked (2026-11-26) for a quick way to enter each day's expenses, with the
-- receipt beside each one. A daily expense is an ordinary expense of Step 34: the same function
-- records it, with the same journal and the same EX- number. Nothing here is a second way of
-- writing an expense. What this adds:
--
--   1. expense_receipts: which stored file (a PDF or a photo, src/modules/files) is the receipt
--      of which expense. Written only by app.attach_expense_receipt, by the owner or an
--      accountant, once; never changed or removed. Whoever sees the expense sees its receipts.
--
--   2. An accountant keeps receipts. Until now only the owner stored a file and only the owner
--      and the auditor read one (drizzle/0002_jobs_files.sql, which says a later step widens
--      this for the roles that work on a document). The policies there are left as they are;
--      policies of this migration's own are added beside them, for the accountant only: to
--      store a file of their own, and to read a file that is their own or is the receipt of an
--      expense they may see. The object store gets the same two rules.
--
--   3. An expense may name nobody. Step 34 asked for a supplier on the list or a payee named in
--      words. A small daily expense (tea, a rickshaw, photocopies) often has no one worth
--      naming, so app.record_expense now takes neither as well, never both. With nobody named
--      the journal and the money's line say what the first line was for, where they said
--      "Paid to ...". Nothing else in the function changes: the text below is 0038's, with only
--      that rule, the constraint beside it, and those two descriptions changed. Tax is withheld
--      only from a supplier on the list, as before.
--
-- No row of any company changes.
--
-- Database error codes (the money range, SE300 to SE399):
--   SE334  (from 0038) no such expense in this company
--   SE376  a receipt is a stored file of the person attaching it, not yet anyone's receipt
--   SE377  an expense has at most ten receipts

CREATE TABLE "expense_receipts" (
	"id" uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
	"tenant_id" uuid NOT NULL,
	"expense_id" uuid NOT NULL,
	"file_id" uuid NOT NULL,
	"created_at" timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
	"created_by" uuid NOT NULL,
	CONSTRAINT "expense_receipts_tenant_id_id_key" UNIQUE("tenant_id","id"),
	CONSTRAINT "expense_receipts_file_key" UNIQUE("tenant_id","file_id")
);
